1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:01,059
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,059 --> 00:00:02,059
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,059 --> 00:00:03,659
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:03,659 --> 00:00:06,792
[Episode 14]

5
00:00:16,195 --> 00:00:18,231
<i>A woman? Are you sure?</i>

6
00:00:18,231 --> 00:00:20,711
It's not like I can't tell
a man from a woman.

7
00:00:20,711 --> 00:00:23,551
That man I saw before,
he really is Kingfisher.

8
00:00:23,551 --> 00:00:25,455
I spotted Kingfisher taking aim,
and got caught.

9
00:00:25,455 --> 00:00:27,219
<i>It's extremely rare for a serial killer</i>

10
00:00:27,219 --> 00:00:30,219
like Kingfisher to suddenly
abandon his beliefs.

11
00:00:30,219 --> 00:00:32,439
Female, estimated to be in her 30s?

12
00:00:32,439 --> 00:00:34,792
<i>Wow. What is this?</i>

13
00:00:36,023 --> 00:00:37,751
Yeah, what is it?

14
00:00:37,751 --> 00:00:39,467
I'm a little busy right now.

15
00:00:55,626 --> 00:00:58,439
[Caller ID Restricted:
Yoo Bo Na is waiting in Seonyudo]

16
00:00:58,439 --> 00:01:00,579
Move out? At this hour?

17
00:01:00,579 --> 00:01:02,171
Where are you going?

18
00:01:02,171 --> 00:01:03,563
What? Seonyudo Island?

19
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:05,311
Wow, even the SWAT team?

20
00:01:05,311 --> 00:01:07,179
That is on another level.

21
00:01:07,179 --> 00:01:09,207
Watch out and stay safe.

22
00:01:09,207 --> 00:01:11,639
Hey, when are you going to meet me?

23
00:01:11,639 --> 00:01:14,192
You said you'd spar with me. Remember?

24
00:01:16,727 --> 00:01:19,215
Tae Seong! Where are you going?

25
00:01:19,215 --> 00:01:20,915
Tae Seong!

26
00:01:27,092 --> 00:01:28,992
[Big Precious]

27
00:01:56,555 --> 00:01:59,467
It's not fair. What we do...

28
00:01:59,467 --> 00:02:01,659
isn't all that different.

29
00:02:01,659 --> 00:02:04,692
I'm warning you.

30
00:02:04,692 --> 00:02:09,335
If you lay a finger on
my husband or my child,

31
00:02:09,335 --> 00:02:11,035
I'll...

32
00:02:11,683 --> 00:02:13,971
make you experience hell
while you're still alive.

33
00:02:13,971 --> 00:02:15,315
Is that so?

34
00:02:15,315 --> 00:02:17,992
Then you can experience hell
while you're alive too.

35
00:02:17,992 --> 00:02:20,839
Get destroyed just like me.

36
00:02:20,839 --> 00:02:23,526
Forget everything you hold dear.

37
00:02:33,351 --> 00:02:36,659
Think you'll still be able to
play the saint then?

38
00:03:04,567 --> 00:03:08,059
Ugh, I'm one step behind again.

39
00:03:37,835 --> 00:03:40,992
Again, our priority is
to take the suspect alive.

40
00:03:40,992 --> 00:03:41,992
Yes, sir.

41
00:03:41,992 --> 00:03:43,159
All units, listen up.

42
00:03:43,159 --> 00:03:46,659
The suspect must be taken alive. Understood?

43
00:03:47,531 --> 00:03:49,455
Teams 1 and 2, this way. Team 3, that way.

44
00:03:49,455 --> 00:03:51,155
Move in!

45
00:04:07,135 --> 00:04:08,531
Why'd you stop?

46
00:04:08,531 --> 00:04:10,326
Keep going!

47
00:04:11,767 --> 00:04:13,395
Try to kill me!

48
00:04:13,395 --> 00:04:15,875
Right in front of your husband.

49
00:04:15,875 --> 00:04:17,892
Just like you always do.

50
00:04:58,175 --> 00:05:00,955
<i>Eleven o'clock!
Suspect believed to be on the rooftop.</i>

51
00:05:00,955 --> 00:05:03,787
Over there! Team 1, follow me.
Team 2, cover us!

52
00:05:03,787 --> 00:05:05,487
Move!

53
00:05:12,259 --> 00:05:16,692
Yoo Bo Na, enjoy rotting in prison
for the rest of your life.

54
00:06:05,055 --> 00:06:07,387
Dong Jin's here. We have to go.

55
00:06:07,387 --> 00:06:09,167
Okay?

56
00:06:09,167 --> 00:06:11,999
We have to go. Hurry. Okay?

57
00:06:11,999 --> 00:06:14,179
Hurry.

58
00:06:14,179 --> 00:06:15,879
Hurry.

59
00:06:25,311 --> 00:06:28,559
<i>What? He knew everything?</i>

60
00:06:29,783 --> 00:06:33,135
<i>If the blade cannot be stopped,
let it come to me.</i>

61
00:06:33,135 --> 00:06:37,092
<i>Let the gun aim only at me.</i>

62
00:06:46,071 --> 00:06:47,792
Keep a close watch on the surroundings.

63
00:07:05,083 --> 00:07:06,783
Honey...

64
00:07:08,019 --> 00:07:09,719
Honey!

65
00:07:15,491 --> 00:07:17,726
Honey, what do I do?

66
00:07:20,879 --> 00:07:22,139
<i>What do I do? Honey...</i>

67
00:07:22,139 --> 00:07:23,839
Ms. Yoo.

68
00:07:33,191 --> 00:07:36,292
It's you, Layla.

69
00:07:37,835 --> 00:07:39,659
Let's get her.

70
00:07:50,731 --> 00:07:52,311
<i>She's not inside the building.</i>

71
00:07:52,311 --> 00:07:54,011
<i>She's not here either.</i>

72
00:08:01,643 --> 00:08:02,827
<i>Northern end of the park.</i>

73
00:08:02,827 --> 00:08:04,726
<i>Suspect spotted near the Han River area.</i>

74
00:08:04,726 --> 00:08:06,815
She's heading toward Seonyu Bridge.

75
00:08:06,815 --> 00:08:08,315
Everyone, move that way!

76
00:08:08,315 --> 00:08:10,026
Darn it.

77
00:08:38,036 --> 00:08:40,226
Let's get out of here first.

78
00:09:06,389 --> 00:09:09,167
Suspect spotted. The suspect
is armed with what appears to be a firearm.

79
00:09:09,167 --> 00:09:11,226
Secure her before she leaves the park.

80
00:09:35,447 --> 00:09:38,539
[No Entry]

81
00:09:44,095 --> 00:09:47,935
We're the ones who should be thanking you
for inviting us into your home.

82
00:09:50,367 --> 00:09:51,703
Look how we meet.

83
00:09:51,703 --> 00:09:53,403
Come with me.

84
00:09:57,883 --> 00:09:59,583
This way.

85
00:10:00,553 --> 00:10:02,526
Watch your step. It's slippery.

86
00:10:22,435 --> 00:10:25,875
Kwon Tae Seong seems to have made his choice.

87
00:10:25,875 --> 00:10:27,892
Now, it's Yoo Bo Na's turn.

88
00:10:38,231 --> 00:10:39,931
Freeze!

89
00:10:40,765 --> 00:10:42,465
Police!

90
00:10:53,827 --> 00:10:56,075
Drop your weapon and put your hands up!

91
00:10:56,075 --> 00:10:57,775
Hurry!

92
00:10:58,711 --> 00:11:00,826
It's all over now, Kingfisher.

93
00:11:01,839 --> 00:11:03,539
Drop the gun.

94
00:11:05,155 --> 00:11:07,026
Kingfisher?

95
00:11:08,703 --> 00:11:10,403
Yoo Bo Na...

96
00:11:12,187 --> 00:11:15,259
You're darn lucky.

97
00:11:15,259 --> 00:11:17,026
Darn it.

98
00:11:33,243 --> 00:11:34,992
Ceasefire!

99
00:11:36,035 --> 00:11:37,859
Ceasefire!

100
00:12:11,659 --> 00:12:15,492
As you know, we can't take her
to a regular hospital.

101
00:12:17,215 --> 00:12:18,915
Okay.

102
00:12:41,859 --> 00:12:43,559
Take her inside.

103
00:12:45,344 --> 00:12:46,827
Director Yoo!

104
00:12:46,827 --> 00:12:49,059
Get ready, hurry.

105
00:12:51,715 --> 00:12:53,426
She'll be all right.

106
00:12:56,323 --> 00:12:58,023
[No Entry]

107
00:12:59,211 --> 00:13:00,911
Tae Seong.

108
00:13:01,595 --> 00:13:06,047
There are people who help
where they're needed.

109
00:13:06,047 --> 00:13:07,747
She's going to be okay.

110
00:13:08,843 --> 00:13:10,543
Okay.

111
00:13:20,867 --> 00:13:22,911
[Operating Room]

112
00:13:52,087 --> 00:13:53,787
Have a seat.

113
00:14:13,823 --> 00:14:18,275
Luckily, only the muscle was damaged.
The vital organs were unharmed.

114
00:14:18,275 --> 00:14:21,659
She'll be fine with some rest.

115
00:14:22,851 --> 00:14:24,551
Thank you.

116
00:14:34,155 --> 00:14:35,855
Mr. Lee!

117
00:14:37,795 --> 00:14:39,843
The NFS team is all standing by.

118
00:14:39,843 --> 00:14:43,026
It's a serious case, so the director
will conduct the autopsy personally.

119
00:14:43,026 --> 00:14:45,627
Man, we'll be up all night
if we're doing an autopsy, then.

120
00:14:45,627 --> 00:14:47,855
Anything unusual
while you were keeping watch?

121
00:14:47,855 --> 00:14:50,055
Any suspicious activity?

122
00:14:50,055 --> 00:14:51,427
No, nothing in particular.

123
00:14:51,427 --> 00:14:53,559
Is something bothering you?

124
00:14:55,192 --> 00:15:00,626
I don't know what I missed
or what I'm missing.

125
00:15:08,955 --> 00:15:10,692
Why did you do it?

126
00:15:12,119 --> 00:15:13,819
Huh?

127
00:15:15,075 --> 00:15:18,159
Why did you take the bullet for me...

128
00:15:20,331 --> 00:15:22,635
How am I supposed to live

129
00:15:22,635 --> 00:15:25,092
if something happens to you?

130
00:15:27,051 --> 00:15:31,759
Without you... how am I supposed to live?

131
00:16:08,926 --> 00:16:11,259
[Chief Na Guk Jin]

132
00:16:12,026 --> 00:16:13,759
[Decline]

133
00:16:21,743 --> 00:16:24,059
<i>Hey, Kwon Tae Seong,
why aren't you answering?</i>

134
00:16:24,059 --> 00:16:25,251
<i>Don't tell me you're still asleep?</i>

135
00:16:25,251 --> 00:16:27,855
<i>Kingfisher was shot
and killed by the police last night.</i>

136
00:16:27,855 --> 00:16:30,359
<i>Hey, get over there. The NFS or
the police headquarters, wherever.</i>

137
00:16:30,359 --> 00:16:31,415
[Breaking News: Kingfisher Killed by Police]

138
00:16:31,415 --> 00:16:35,959
<i>Serial sniper Kingfisher
was killed last night.</i>

139
00:16:35,959 --> 00:16:38,792
<i>Enjoy rotting in prison
for the rest of your life.</i>

140
00:16:43,063 --> 00:16:46,191
<i>According to reports,
Kingfisher was shot and killed</i>

141
00:16:46,191 --> 00:16:49,126
<i>after a chase with police at an undisclosed
location in Seoul last night.</i>

142
00:16:49,126 --> 00:16:52,159
<i>Kingfisher's identity, which had
remained a mystery for 15 years,</i>

143
00:16:52,159 --> 00:16:54,331
<i>has unexpectedly been revealed
to be a woman in her 30s.</i>

144
00:16:54,331 --> 00:16:57,192
<i>The revelation has shocked
and confused the public.</i>

145
00:16:57,192 --> 00:16:58,192
You're from the NFS, right?

146
00:16:58,192 --> 00:16:59,715
Has Kingfisher's identity been confirmed?

147
00:16:59,715 --> 00:17:01,631
Who is she? Please release
her name and photo.

148
00:17:01,631 --> 00:17:03,159
Why was she killed instead of taken alive?

149
00:17:03,159 --> 00:17:06,192
Are you certain the woman in her 30s
who died at the scene was Kingfisher?

150
00:17:06,192 --> 00:17:07,826
Was there any excessive
use of force by the police?

151
00:17:07,826 --> 00:17:10,559
Will we never know Kingfisher's motive?

152
00:17:12,647 --> 00:17:13,783
Finally got her.

153
00:17:13,783 --> 00:17:16,855
Good work.

154
00:17:16,855 --> 00:17:18,959
Finally got her.

155
00:17:22,939 --> 00:17:24,951
Good job.

156
00:17:24,951 --> 00:17:26,775
But what do you mean we can't identify her?

157
00:17:26,775 --> 00:17:30,587
Her fingerprints and DNA don't match
anything in our national databases.

158
00:17:30,587 --> 00:17:33,091
We checked with Immigration as well,

159
00:17:33,091 --> 00:17:35,567
but there are no matching fingerprints
from any foreign national.

160
00:17:35,567 --> 00:17:38,275
So what, did she enter the country illegally?

161
00:17:38,275 --> 00:17:43,126
We've requested an identity check
through Interpol channels for now.

162
00:17:43,126 --> 00:17:44,126
Oh, man.

163
00:17:44,126 --> 00:17:46,615
Nothing about this is ever straightforward.

164
00:17:46,615 --> 00:17:49,192
Still, at least we've got her.

165
00:17:49,867 --> 00:17:51,259
Well done.

166
00:17:51,259 --> 00:17:52,959
Good work.

167
00:17:54,226 --> 00:17:56,679
[Commissioner General]

168
00:17:56,679 --> 00:17:58,999
Calls are blowing up everywhere.

169
00:17:58,999 --> 00:18:00,699
Yes, Commissioner.

170
00:18:29,192 --> 00:18:30,892
Honey!

171
00:18:32,231 --> 00:18:34,019
Are you okay?

172
00:18:34,019 --> 00:18:36,103
Are you all right?

173
00:18:36,103 --> 00:18:37,827
You've been through so much.

174
00:18:37,827 --> 00:18:40,579
Does anything hurt? Any discomfort?

175
00:18:40,579 --> 00:18:42,926
Should I get the doctor?

176
00:18:46,511 --> 00:18:48,626
Honey, if you get up now...

177
00:18:54,039 --> 00:18:56,626
Could you get the team leader for me?

178
00:18:59,491 --> 00:19:01,191
Okay.

179
00:19:06,387 --> 00:19:09,871
Is Director Yoo okay? Is she awake?

180
00:19:09,871 --> 00:19:11,571
Yes.

181
00:19:14,987 --> 00:19:17,992
Team Leader, Bo Na's looking for you.

182
00:19:30,787 --> 00:19:34,035
Yeah, Se Ah. I don't think
I can make it home today.

183
00:19:34,035 --> 00:19:37,147
<i>Alright. I'll have her sleep over
at my place tonight.</i>

184
00:19:37,147 --> 00:19:38,847
Please take care of her.

185
00:19:51,043 --> 00:19:52,743
Honey, what are you doing?

186
00:19:53,707 --> 00:19:55,559
Why? Where are you going?

187
00:19:57,461 --> 00:20:00,692
You already knew, didn't you?

188
00:20:03,051 --> 00:20:04,392
It was from that day on.

189
00:20:04,392 --> 00:20:06,859
The day Yul went to the ER.

190
00:20:06,859 --> 00:20:09,192
You kept avoiding my eyes,

191
00:20:10,031 --> 00:20:12,959
looking at me like I was a stranger.

192
00:20:18,947 --> 00:20:21,626
That's why you came home late for a while

193
00:20:21,626 --> 00:20:24,792
and couldn't eat or sleep properly.

194
00:20:25,763 --> 00:20:27,943
- Honey, I...
- That must have been tough for you.

195
00:20:27,943 --> 00:20:29,595
Honey, just hear me out for a second.

196
00:20:29,595 --> 00:20:31,392
You were angry, too, weren't you?

197
00:20:31,392 --> 00:20:35,487
At the wife who's been lying
to you all this time, weren't you?

198
00:20:37,259 --> 00:20:39,527
You must've been

199
00:20:39,527 --> 00:20:41,759
confused and lost.

200
00:20:45,147 --> 00:20:46,847
I was.

201
00:20:49,899 --> 00:20:52,115
I was angry,

202
00:20:52,115 --> 00:20:54,392
confused, and completely lost.

203
00:20:55,187 --> 00:20:58,363
Honestly, your secret was
too much for me. I was scared.

204
00:20:58,363 --> 00:20:59,892
But...

205
00:20:59,892 --> 00:21:02,726
I've come to one conclusion. To protect you.

206
00:21:04,059 --> 00:21:07,259
To protect you and our family.

207
00:21:09,191 --> 00:21:11,739
Honey, can't we just go back to how we were?

208
00:21:11,739 --> 00:21:13,439
We can smile again

209
00:21:15,407 --> 00:21:18,092
and act like nothing ever happened.

210
00:21:21,235 --> 00:21:23,492
Pretend none of this happened?

211
00:21:31,923 --> 00:21:34,059
I don't think I can do that.

212
00:21:38,715 --> 00:21:43,227
Every time you look at me,
you'll think about who I really am.

213
00:21:43,227 --> 00:21:47,092
You'll find me strange,
and you'll be confused and in pain.

214
00:21:50,892 --> 00:21:54,467
You'll be constantly wondering
when everything's going to blow up.

215
00:21:54,467 --> 00:21:57,092
No. That's not going to happen.

216
00:21:57,092 --> 00:21:58,687
I'll become your living hell.

217
00:21:58,687 --> 00:22:00,059
No, honey.

218
00:22:00,059 --> 00:22:02,459
No, please don't do this...

219
00:22:10,311 --> 00:22:12,459
I can't go back to the way things were.

220
00:22:15,623 --> 00:22:18,192
You still don't truly know me.

221
00:22:52,827 --> 00:22:54,047
Honey!

222
00:22:54,047 --> 00:22:56,266
Honey, wait...

223
00:22:56,266 --> 00:22:57,966
Honey!

224
00:24:00,363 --> 00:24:02,563
<i>I can't go back to the way things were.</i>

225
00:24:02,563 --> 00:24:04,739
<i>You still don't truly know me.</i>

226
00:24:04,739 --> 00:24:08,423
Director Yoo has submitted her resignation.

227
00:24:08,423 --> 00:24:11,139
We suggested sick leave
or a leave of absence,

228
00:24:11,139 --> 00:24:13,559
but I think she's made up her mind.

229
00:24:34,971 --> 00:24:36,671
Mr. Kwon Tae Seong.

230
00:24:42,143 --> 00:24:44,691
I stopped by on my way to the airport.

231
00:24:44,691 --> 00:24:46,827
I'm sorry.

232
00:24:46,827 --> 00:24:49,451
I should've acted sooner.

233
00:24:49,451 --> 00:24:52,059
Could that gunshot have...

234
00:24:53,311 --> 00:24:56,111
Mama sent me to protect her.

235
00:24:56,111 --> 00:24:58,959
I'm probably going to get an earful
from her when I get back.

236
00:25:01,267 --> 00:25:03,926
Is Bo Na going with you?

237
00:25:08,211 --> 00:25:10,551
I know from experience.

238
00:25:10,551 --> 00:25:13,915
Just mentioning her husband or child

239
00:25:13,915 --> 00:25:16,823
makes Yoo Bo Na's eyes go wild.

240
00:25:16,823 --> 00:25:18,547
For someone like that...

241
00:25:18,547 --> 00:25:21,692
I asked her a few times, just in case,

242
00:25:21,692 --> 00:25:23,787
but she flat-out refused.

243
00:25:23,787 --> 00:25:26,159
She'd disappoint the person waiting for her.

244
00:25:31,475 --> 00:25:34,927
I meant it when I said Bo Na seemed

245
00:25:34,927 --> 00:25:36,951
to have found a good guy.

246
00:25:36,951 --> 00:25:39,591
I told her the same thing.

247
00:25:39,591 --> 00:25:44,031
Well, she probably knows that
better than anyone.

248
00:25:44,031 --> 00:25:45,731
So...

249
00:25:52,879 --> 00:25:54,579
Thank you.

250
00:26:09,067 --> 00:26:11,092
Please take care of it.

251
00:26:31,215 --> 00:26:34,192
I sent these flowers to Cheol today.

252
00:26:34,192 --> 00:26:36,199
They're called marguerites.

253
00:26:36,199 --> 00:26:38,483
They look a lot like
cosmos flowers, don't they?

254
00:26:38,483 --> 00:26:42,003
So customers often confuse them.

255
00:26:42,003 --> 00:26:44,559
What is their flower language?

256
00:26:45,859 --> 00:26:48,055
"Revealing a secret."

257
00:26:48,055 --> 00:26:49,983
"True love."

258
00:26:49,983 --> 00:26:52,759
"True love has no secrets."

259
00:26:52,759 --> 00:26:55,692
"True love means revealing the truth."

260
00:26:56,387 --> 00:26:58,659
That's what I thought it meant.

261
00:26:58,659 --> 00:27:02,839
But someone told me that
the meaning wasn't very nice.

262
00:27:02,839 --> 00:27:06,259
Sometimes you keep secrets
because you love someone too much.

263
00:27:07,447 --> 00:27:10,127
<i>He's someone who lives in the light.</i>

264
00:27:10,127 --> 00:27:12,426
<i>Because he's different from me.</i>

265
00:27:13,035 --> 00:27:16,859
Because if he knew how different we are,
we couldn't stay together.

266
00:27:18,603 --> 00:27:20,711
I'm not worried.

267
00:27:20,711 --> 00:27:22,559
Because that day will never come.

268
00:27:23,855 --> 00:27:27,059
Because the day he sees my other side

269
00:27:27,827 --> 00:27:29,826
will never come.

270
00:27:30,526 --> 00:27:32,919
<i>Back then, I thought it was confidence</i>

271
00:27:32,919 --> 00:27:35,059
that she'd never
let her secret be discovered,

272
00:27:35,059 --> 00:27:39,259
but thinking about it now,
I think it was anxiety.

273
00:27:41,611 --> 00:27:45,983
A promise she was making
to herself not to be afraid.

274
00:27:45,983 --> 00:27:50,859
Because she already knew how it would end.

275
00:27:52,887 --> 00:27:55,627
Maybe she'd already decided

276
00:27:55,627 --> 00:27:59,135
from the beginning how this would end

277
00:27:59,135 --> 00:28:01,892
when the moment came.

278
00:28:04,159 --> 00:28:06,992
That's what I've come to think.

279
00:28:14,426 --> 00:28:17,692
[Forensic DNA profile comparison]

280
00:28:21,407 --> 00:28:23,626
Kingfisher Task Force.

281
00:28:25,091 --> 00:28:26,792
Oh, yes.

282
00:28:28,027 --> 00:28:30,095
Did we hear back from Interpol?

283
00:28:30,095 --> 00:28:31,992
Yes, thank you.

284
00:28:33,459 --> 00:28:35,626
Mr. Lee, International Cooperation says

285
00:28:35,626 --> 00:28:39,359
they found a DNA match
for the body found in Russia.

286
00:28:39,359 --> 00:28:40,359
Russia?

287
00:28:40,359 --> 00:28:42,967
[DNA Match Search Against
Russian Federation Records]

288
00:28:42,967 --> 00:28:46,259
"Layla Choi, age 38."

289
00:28:46,259 --> 00:28:48,595
"Reported missing approximately
15 years ago."

290
00:28:48,595 --> 00:28:50,831
"No record of her whereabouts since?"

291
00:28:50,831 --> 00:28:54,799
Fifteen years... That lines up with
Kingfisher's active period, right?

292
00:28:54,799 --> 00:28:56,863
Man, then that's pretty conclusive.

293
00:28:56,863 --> 00:28:58,692
So her name was Layla?

294
00:28:58,692 --> 00:29:01,615
So she must have entered illegally
15 years ago

295
00:29:01,615 --> 00:29:03,959
and lived as an undocumented resident.

296
00:29:07,692 --> 00:29:09,775
Doesn't something feel off?

297
00:29:09,775 --> 00:29:11,635
What do you mean?

298
00:29:11,635 --> 00:29:14,899
Oh, you mean the other DNA from the hair?

299
00:29:14,899 --> 00:29:18,335
Well, that could've
belonged to an accomplice.

300
00:29:18,335 --> 00:29:24,292
But why would she go to that park alone
in the middle of the night?

301
00:29:25,551 --> 00:29:27,515
Exactly.

302
00:29:27,515 --> 00:29:29,759
Maybe she went there to meet someone?

303
00:29:29,759 --> 00:29:32,927
But the park was closed at that hour.
There shouldn't have been anyone there.

304
00:29:32,927 --> 00:29:34,627
You're right.

305
00:29:36,075 --> 00:29:38,726
There shouldn't have been anyone.

306
00:29:42,815 --> 00:29:44,859
Oh, you're here?

307
00:29:44,859 --> 00:29:45,887
Yeah, where's Yul?

308
00:29:45,887 --> 00:29:47,999
She's already asleep. Look at the time.

309
00:29:47,999 --> 00:29:49,926
Let her sleep here tonight.

310
00:29:50,967 --> 00:29:52,667
Mom...

311
00:30:02,735 --> 00:30:05,792
Where's Yul's mom?

312
00:30:06,907 --> 00:30:09,955
I told you. She's away on
a long-term business trip overseas.

313
00:30:09,955 --> 00:30:11,139
All of a sudden?

314
00:30:11,139 --> 00:30:12,363
Where overseas?

315
00:30:12,363 --> 00:30:14,219
When's she coming back?

316
00:30:14,219 --> 00:30:16,807
Look at that guilty look on his face.

317
00:30:16,807 --> 00:30:18,203
He's terrible at lying.

318
00:30:18,203 --> 00:30:19,762
I knew something was wrong

319
00:30:19,762 --> 00:30:22,466
when he came home
looking so pale and worn out.

320
00:30:22,466 --> 00:30:26,207
Tell me. What on earth did you do to Bo Na?

321
00:30:26,207 --> 00:30:28,051
- Huh?
- Huh?

322
00:30:28,051 --> 00:30:30,863
Did you throw a tantrum because she
put her job before you and the kid?

323
00:30:30,863 --> 00:30:33,783
What kind of world do you think this is?

324
00:30:33,783 --> 00:30:35,275
He still hasn't come to his senses.

325
00:30:35,275 --> 00:30:37,299
I definitely think
you're the one who messed up.

326
00:30:37,299 --> 00:30:38,783
Exactly. That's what I'm saying!

327
00:30:38,783 --> 00:30:40,871
When she first got married,

328
00:30:40,871 --> 00:30:43,859
I gave her a hard time
for being bad with a knife,

329
00:30:43,859 --> 00:30:46,251
and a month later, she showed up
with calluses on her hands.

330
00:30:46,251 --> 00:30:48,287
She must've chopped enough
to wear her hands out.

331
00:30:48,287 --> 00:30:50,411
Back then, she didn't even know
who Hyun Bin was, so I gave her a weird look.

332
00:30:50,411 --> 00:30:53,091
Then she watched everything he was in
and came back reciting his lines.

333
00:30:53,091 --> 00:30:55,991
"Sun Il, I'm not weird anymore, right?"

334
00:30:55,991 --> 00:30:57,447
Even though I never asked her to,

335
00:30:57,447 --> 00:31:00,459
she got life, accident, indemnity,
and dementia insurance

336
00:31:00,459 --> 00:31:03,059
for everyone in her department.

337
00:31:03,059 --> 00:31:04,803
I was top of the sales rankings that month.

338
00:31:04,803 --> 00:31:05,895
- No way!
- Seriously?

339
00:31:05,895 --> 00:31:07,263
Yeah.

340
00:31:07,263 --> 00:31:09,607
That's just the kind of person she is. Okay?

341
00:31:09,607 --> 00:31:12,535
She works herself to the bone
for everything! Okay?

342
00:31:12,535 --> 00:31:14,559
How bad could it have been

343
00:31:14,559 --> 00:31:19,659
for someone so devoted to her family
to leave even Yul behind?

344
00:31:19,659 --> 00:31:23,859
She doesn't have any friends,
so she probably has nowhere to go, either.

345
00:31:25,351 --> 00:31:29,651
Does she have parents
to go back to? Any family?

346
00:31:29,651 --> 00:31:33,383
She has nowhere in this world to go.

347
00:31:33,383 --> 00:31:37,626
What on earth did you do
to make her leave her own home?

348
00:31:38,548 --> 00:31:41,347
Oh, gosh.

349
00:31:41,347 --> 00:31:42,892
- Huh?
- Mom!

350
00:31:42,892 --> 00:31:44,497
- Are you okay?
- Careful.

351
00:31:44,497 --> 00:31:46,275
Mom, your blood pressure's going up.

352
00:31:46,275 --> 00:31:47,491
- Let me see.
- Oh, Mom!

353
00:31:47,491 --> 00:31:49,793
- Bring it down.
- You can't let your blood pressure go up.

354
00:31:49,793 --> 00:31:51,012
Her blood pressure shouldn't go up.
Go buy medicine!

355
00:31:51,012 --> 00:31:52,026
- Quick.
- Quick, get a calming pill.

356
00:31:52,026 --> 00:31:53,555
Mom! Mom, are you okay?

357
00:31:53,555 --> 00:31:57,295
It breaks my heart just thinking about it...

358
00:31:57,295 --> 00:31:59,155
My wife has a lot of people on her side.

359
00:31:59,155 --> 00:32:02,155
Oh, my. Jeez.

360
00:32:11,074 --> 00:32:12,626
<i>She doesn't have any family here.</i>

361
00:32:12,626 --> 00:32:15,043
[Eight Years Ago]

362
00:32:15,043 --> 00:32:17,203
She was adopted by
a Russian family as a child

363
00:32:17,203 --> 00:32:19,692
and came back as an adult.

364
00:32:27,107 --> 00:32:29,767
Please look out for my girlfriend.

365
00:32:29,767 --> 00:32:32,203
Why are you asking me?

366
00:32:32,203 --> 00:32:33,926
You're the one who needs to treat her right.

367
00:32:36,187 --> 00:32:38,359
You said she has no family.

368
00:32:39,279 --> 00:32:41,226
So you take good care of her, buddy.

369
00:32:51,183 --> 00:32:52,883
<i>Suspect spotted.</i>

370
00:33:02,219 --> 00:33:04,392
[Headband, Red Devil, Tall and Slender]

371
00:33:05,926 --> 00:33:08,359
[Short or Tied Hair, Big Bag on Shoulder]

372
00:33:12,343 --> 00:33:14,076
<i>My wife and my child.</i>

373
00:33:14,076 --> 00:33:15,992
My beloved family.

374
00:33:16,835 --> 00:33:18,355
I need to protect them.

375
00:33:18,355 --> 00:33:20,259
You'll be on my side, right?

376
00:33:21,343 --> 00:33:23,159
<i>You said you wanted to repay the favor.</i>

377
00:33:33,692 --> 00:33:36,259
[Not Today]

378
00:33:41,555 --> 00:33:44,043
It must've really shaken him.

379
00:33:44,043 --> 00:33:47,142
He's been completely out of it ever since.

380
00:33:47,142 --> 00:33:52,667
I know. He's been reading nothing
but Kingfisher articles all day.

381
00:33:52,667 --> 00:33:55,292
Maybe he was shocked
to find out she was a woman?

382
00:33:55,292 --> 00:33:59,659
Or is he upset that he missed the scoop?

383
00:34:00,551 --> 00:34:05,059
Well, he must be feeling pretty torn
after looking into it for so long.

384
00:34:05,059 --> 00:34:07,403
Reporters get like that sometimes.

385
00:34:07,403 --> 00:34:09,759
Leave him alone for a while.

386
00:34:09,759 --> 00:34:13,726
[Killed by a Gun, Dead by a Gun:
Kingfisher's Miserable End]

387
00:34:14,959 --> 00:34:18,559
[From Champion of Justice to Brutal Killer:
Kingfisher's Downfall]

388
00:34:20,011 --> 00:34:22,179
I opened the door to serve food in the room,

389
00:34:22,179 --> 00:34:25,335
and the two of them
suddenly stopped whispering.

390
00:34:25,335 --> 00:34:29,263
I got curious, so I stepped outside
and listened through the crack in the door.

391
00:34:29,263 --> 00:34:32,665
"Let's do it abroad. We'll meet there."

392
00:34:32,665 --> 00:34:34,791
They said something like that.

393
00:34:34,791 --> 00:34:38,526
Did you hear what they were planning to do?

394
00:34:39,467 --> 00:34:42,059
I think they mentioned some girl.

395
00:34:42,743 --> 00:34:46,792
Oh, and that it could all be done for money
with no strings attached.

396
00:35:02,087 --> 00:35:04,075
Oh.

397
00:35:04,075 --> 00:35:06,315
Mr. Kwon Tae Seong.

398
00:35:06,315 --> 00:35:09,192
Good to see you. Please come in.

399
00:35:15,107 --> 00:35:19,787
In the past, Director Yoo
said she wanted to quit.

400
00:35:19,787 --> 00:35:21,943
We all tried to talk her out of it.

401
00:35:21,943 --> 00:35:24,415
Because everyone worried that

402
00:35:24,415 --> 00:35:27,815
she might literally die
if she kept going like that.

403
00:35:27,815 --> 00:35:29,526
Director Yoo kept

404
00:35:30,783 --> 00:35:32,792
moving forward

405
00:35:33,892 --> 00:35:35,726
with one thing in mind.

406
00:35:36,859 --> 00:35:38,692
She believed that if she kept at it,

407
00:35:39,959 --> 00:35:42,791
the world would get a little better.

408
00:35:42,791 --> 00:35:44,035
A little safer.

409
00:35:44,035 --> 00:35:45,759
But...

410
00:35:46,435 --> 00:35:49,226
does the world really get better that easily?

411
00:35:49,979 --> 00:35:56,459
That's what made Director Yoo
the most exhausted and worn out.

412
00:36:00,919 --> 00:36:03,643
Huh? Hold on! Wait!

413
00:36:03,643 --> 00:36:06,392
We made her take an extended leave

414
00:36:07,307 --> 00:36:10,047
to give her some time
to get her life back on track.

415
00:36:10,047 --> 00:36:11,747
If she still felt the same

416
00:36:12,555 --> 00:36:17,027
after she came back,
we promised we wouldn't try to stop her.

417
00:36:17,027 --> 00:36:19,339
But three or four months later,

418
00:36:19,339 --> 00:36:23,892
she came back and asked us
to tear up her resignation.

419
00:36:34,635 --> 00:36:39,392
I think Director Yoo still needs
that kind of time right now.

420
00:36:40,131 --> 00:36:45,326
So think of it as giving her a long trip.

421
00:36:46,055 --> 00:36:51,059
And maybe, just like when the two of you
first met at a desperate time,

422
00:36:51,799 --> 00:36:54,426
another chance will come

423
00:36:55,715 --> 00:36:58,392
<i>when you need each other just as badly.</i>

424
00:37:06,992 --> 00:37:08,959
[Detective Lee Dong Jin]

425
00:37:16,251 --> 00:37:17,895
What's up this late?

426
00:37:17,895 --> 00:37:21,163
<i>Well, just thought of you.</i>

427
00:37:21,163 --> 00:37:23,151
<i>What are you doing?</i>

428
00:37:23,151 --> 00:37:26,227
My wife and Yul wanted ice cream,

429
00:37:26,227 --> 00:37:28,275
so I went to the convenience store.
I'm heading home now.

430
00:37:28,275 --> 00:37:29,467
Ice cream?

431
00:37:29,467 --> 00:37:31,167
At this hour?

432
00:37:31,867 --> 00:37:33,692
They wanted some.

433
00:37:35,751 --> 00:37:38,727
Then evening training will be tough
while you're looking after Yul.

434
00:37:38,727 --> 00:37:40,892
Alright, keep in touch.

435
00:37:42,451 --> 00:37:43,555
What about Yul?

436
00:37:43,555 --> 00:37:45,825
Well, Se Ah's sister-in-law went somewhere,

437
00:37:45,825 --> 00:37:47,587
so she's staying at Se Ah's for a while.

438
00:37:47,587 --> 00:37:50,263
Ms. Bo Na? Where did she go?

439
00:37:50,263 --> 00:37:53,093
Her brother says she went on
a long business trip overseas,

440
00:37:53,093 --> 00:37:54,992
but Se Ah isn't so sure.

441
00:37:54,992 --> 00:37:56,902
Maybe something happened between them.

442
00:37:56,902 --> 00:37:59,192
<i>Things haven't seemed great at home lately.</i>

443
00:38:00,807 --> 00:38:02,507
Hello?

444
00:38:04,230 --> 00:38:06,315
[Detective Lee Dong Jin]
Why call and say nothing?

445
00:38:06,315 --> 00:38:08,979
Hello? Lee Dong Jin!

446
00:38:08,979 --> 00:38:10,935
You...

447
00:38:10,935 --> 00:38:12,587
I'm going to ask you one important question,

448
00:38:12,587 --> 00:38:15,226
so think carefully before you answer.

449
00:38:17,551 --> 00:38:19,235
What now? What is it?

450
00:38:19,235 --> 00:38:22,303
Who do you like more, me or your wife?

451
00:38:22,303 --> 00:38:24,003
You crazy punk, are you drunk?

452
00:38:24,003 --> 00:38:25,263
<i>I'm serious right now.</i>

453
00:38:25,263 --> 00:38:27,871
Of course, I love my Bo Na.

454
00:38:27,871 --> 00:38:30,435
I could live just fine without you
for a thousand years.

455
00:38:30,435 --> 00:38:33,735
But I couldn't live a single day
without my Bo Na.

456
00:38:33,735 --> 00:38:36,292
You mean that? Really?

457
00:38:36,292 --> 00:38:37,892
You don't regret it, right?

458
00:38:37,892 --> 00:38:39,043
<i>No.</i>

459
00:38:39,043 --> 00:38:41,726
Ask me a hundred times.
My answer won't change.

460
00:38:43,926 --> 00:38:48,692
The best thing I ever did
was meet Bo Na, marry her...

461
00:38:50,251 --> 00:38:52,126
and start a family.

462
00:38:59,303 --> 00:39:01,326
Ugh, hang up, you crazy punk!

463
00:39:45,392 --> 00:39:48,159
[Mommy, I miss you. I love you so much]

464
00:39:52,527 --> 00:39:54,767
<i>Which one did you like best?</i>

465
00:39:54,767 --> 00:39:58,459
<i>Well... I loved them all.
I loved every moment.</i>

466
00:39:58,459 --> 00:39:59,687
[Six Years Ago, Summer]

467
00:39:59,687 --> 00:40:01,194
- This is so nice!
- There are so many

468
00:40:01,194 --> 00:40:02,992
- pretty things over there.
- Here?

469
00:40:03,775 --> 00:40:06,426
Okay, one, two!

470
00:40:09,523 --> 00:40:11,379
Stand here.

471
00:40:11,379 --> 00:40:13,627
Me?

472
00:40:13,627 --> 00:40:15,011
- Princess Yoo Bo Na!
- What?

473
00:40:15,011 --> 00:40:17,099
Stay classy.

474
00:40:17,099 --> 00:40:18,587
- It's dangerous, right?
- Yeah.

475
00:40:18,587 --> 00:40:20,171
Strike a pose.

476
00:40:20,171 --> 00:40:23,319
One, two, three!

477
00:40:23,319 --> 00:40:25,635
Take a picture in a beautiful setting.

478
00:40:25,635 --> 00:40:27,635
Did we complete today's mission?

479
00:40:27,635 --> 00:40:30,126
- Mission complete!
- Okay, great.

480
00:40:30,747 --> 00:40:32,038
What should we do next?

481
00:40:32,038 --> 00:40:35,251
Next? Well...

482
00:40:35,251 --> 00:40:40,227
Oh! How about making jjajang ramyeon
at home on Sunday?

483
00:40:40,227 --> 00:40:43,089
You know, the Sunday jjajang ramyeon chef.

484
00:40:43,089 --> 00:40:44,243
Please make that for me.

485
00:40:44,243 --> 00:40:45,251
Alright.

486
00:40:45,251 --> 00:40:46,459
- What else?
- Well...

487
00:40:46,459 --> 00:40:49,031
- Having strawberry shakes for dessert!
- Okay.

488
00:40:49,031 --> 00:40:50,723
Watching a late-night movie. A horror movie.

489
00:40:50,723 --> 00:40:51,992
- Oh, sounds good!
- How about that?

490
00:40:51,992 --> 00:40:54,571
- You can handle that, right?
- No.

491
00:40:54,571 --> 00:40:58,207
Then we'll have a picnic
by the Han River and eat fried chicken.

492
00:40:58,207 --> 00:40:59,626
We've got so much to do.

493
00:40:59,626 --> 00:41:01,071
We'd better get busy, then.

494
00:41:01,071 --> 00:41:02,663
Tae Seong, is there anything you want to do?

495
00:41:02,663 --> 00:41:04,363
I want to get married.

496
00:41:07,567 --> 00:41:10,611
Marriage is a bit early for you, huh?

497
00:41:10,611 --> 00:41:12,311
Oh...

498
00:41:16,126 --> 00:41:19,751
But when people do this, don't they...

499
00:41:19,751 --> 00:41:22,439
do it while giving something?

500
00:41:22,439 --> 00:41:24,555
This is a proposal, right?

501
00:41:24,555 --> 00:41:25,747
On TV, when people do this,

502
00:41:25,747 --> 00:41:28,075
- they always give something.
- Oh, well...

503
00:41:28,075 --> 00:41:29,427
Oh, I mean...

504
00:41:29,427 --> 00:41:32,299
This isn't an official proposal.

505
00:41:32,299 --> 00:41:36,091
It's just that everything I'd been
keeping bottled up inside...

506
00:41:36,091 --> 00:41:37,232
It just came spilling out.

507
00:41:37,232 --> 00:41:39,579
But I was planning
to make a proper proposal...

508
00:41:39,579 --> 00:41:43,163
I had a ring all ready to give you...

509
00:41:43,163 --> 00:41:44,863
Okay.

510
00:41:48,415 --> 00:41:50,019
But...

511
00:41:50,019 --> 00:41:51,719
Well...

512
00:41:52,443 --> 00:41:54,459
When are you going to do it?

513
00:41:56,331 --> 00:41:58,899
Once you've picked a date,
let me know beforehand.

514
00:41:58,899 --> 00:42:04,003
That way, I can think about
what I'm going to say.

515
00:42:04,003 --> 00:42:06,192
Be sure to tell me the date.

516
00:42:12,619 --> 00:42:14,792
Tae Seong, come on.

517
00:42:20,967 --> 00:42:24,327
<i>There's still so much I want to do with you.</i>

518
00:42:24,327 --> 00:42:25,327
Really?

519
00:42:25,327 --> 00:42:30,891
Something we haven't done before.
Something better and more special.

520
00:42:30,891 --> 00:42:35,099
Let's do every single one of them together.

521
00:42:35,099 --> 00:42:37,091
Yeah.

522
00:42:37,091 --> 00:42:38,791
Together.

523
00:43:22,843 --> 00:43:23,871
Mr. Kwon!

524
00:43:23,871 --> 00:43:26,795
Your hunch was right.

525
00:43:26,795 --> 00:43:29,985
The two Kingfisher victims
were both in Cambodia

526
00:43:29,985 --> 00:43:32,003
[Booking Information]
around the same time last summer.

527
00:43:32,003 --> 00:43:34,192
And this.

528
00:43:34,192 --> 00:43:37,671
And during that time, a mom
and daughter selling food on the street

529
00:43:37,671 --> 00:43:40,095
were murdered in Cambodia.

530
00:43:40,095 --> 00:43:42,759
Their bodies were found,

531
00:43:43,467 --> 00:43:45,243
but the killer was never caught?

532
00:43:45,243 --> 00:43:47,867
Please prepare a travel request.
Four days and three nights in Cambodia.

533
00:43:47,867 --> 00:43:49,892
Okay, understood.

534
00:43:51,426 --> 00:43:53,492
[Detective Lee Dong Jin]

535
00:43:56,535 --> 00:43:58,855
Detective Lee Dong Jin,

536
00:43:58,855 --> 00:44:02,992
let's wrap up this case properly together.

537
00:44:12,959 --> 00:44:15,499
- Darn it.
- Kwon Se Ah, you've still got it.

538
00:44:15,499 --> 00:44:18,026
Of course, I'll be looking sharp
as a cop soon too.

539
00:44:18,026 --> 00:44:20,335
Come on. You're taking
the police too lightly.

540
00:44:20,335 --> 00:44:23,115
It is easy. Even a guy
who got thrown by a tiny girl

541
00:44:23,115 --> 00:44:25,935
and whined to keep it a secret is a cop now.

542
00:44:25,935 --> 00:44:27,792
How long are you going to bring that up...

543
00:44:30,827 --> 00:44:32,263
Hey, that's a cheap move!

544
00:44:32,263 --> 00:44:34,359
That's why you need to focus.

545
00:44:41,643 --> 00:44:43,211
That was dangerous just now.
Stay focused, okay?

546
00:44:43,211 --> 00:44:45,179
Darn it. I told you not to go easy on me!

547
00:44:45,179 --> 00:44:46,892
Are you going to do judo with your mouth?

548
00:45:04,659 --> 00:45:07,659
Oh!

549
00:45:13,959 --> 00:45:17,359
Ugh, I almost died doing judo.

550
00:45:18,559 --> 00:45:20,743
Hey, this is exactly why I told you not to.

551
00:45:20,743 --> 00:45:22,926
What are you doing in a sacred judo gym?

552
00:45:22,926 --> 00:45:23,926
Hey, what did I do?

553
00:45:23,926 --> 00:45:25,926
What are you doing?
This is a judo gym, not a wrestling ring.

554
00:45:25,926 --> 00:45:28,159
You went easy on me, didn't you?

555
00:45:42,619 --> 00:45:44,316
How's the competition prep going?

556
00:45:44,316 --> 00:45:50,326
Oh... It's been so long since I quit.
I'm just getting my feel back.

557
00:45:50,979 --> 00:45:53,859
You look like you could win
even if you competed today.

558
00:45:54,507 --> 00:45:56,459
I saw it myself.

559
00:45:57,826 --> 00:46:00,527
But that was real combat.

560
00:46:00,527 --> 00:46:03,192
Competition is different.

561
00:46:05,315 --> 00:46:08,292
You said you wanted to find out
what kind of person you are, right?

562
00:46:18,059 --> 00:46:20,130
From what I've seen,

563
00:46:20,130 --> 00:46:23,311
you're bright, honest, and brave.

564
00:46:23,311 --> 00:46:25,763
Decent and upright...

565
00:46:25,763 --> 00:46:29,481
Well, that's more or less right.

566
00:46:29,481 --> 00:46:34,279
You probably already
have a sense of what I'm like.

567
00:46:34,279 --> 00:46:36,471
So I think...

568
00:46:36,471 --> 00:46:40,111
you're probably thinking the same thing I am.

569
00:46:40,111 --> 00:46:42,207
The same...

570
00:46:42,207 --> 00:46:44,326
What are you thinking about?

571
00:46:45,495 --> 00:46:50,195
I guess we can't look toward the same future.

572
00:46:50,195 --> 00:46:51,895
That's what I was thinking.

573
00:46:54,423 --> 00:46:56,643
I was really glad to have met you.

574
00:46:56,643 --> 00:46:58,935
During our time together,

575
00:46:58,935 --> 00:47:00,695
I had so much fun.

576
00:47:03,647 --> 00:47:07,792
You'll become a great police officer.

577
00:47:07,792 --> 00:47:11,726
I'll always be cheering you on from afar.

578
00:47:26,759 --> 00:47:29,419
I'll make sure I become
a good police officer.

579
00:47:29,419 --> 00:47:31,626
Thank you, Assistant Manager Ki.

580
00:47:36,543 --> 00:47:40,071
If I leave again someday,
will you follow me then too?

581
00:47:40,071 --> 00:47:41,771
Are you going somewhere?

582
00:47:44,924 --> 00:47:46,311
Where would I even go?

583
00:47:46,311 --> 00:47:47,843
<i>Everything I need is right here.</i>

584
00:47:47,843 --> 00:47:51,492
She went alone this time.

585
00:47:57,023 --> 00:47:58,975
Stop moping around, and get up.

586
00:47:58,975 --> 00:48:00,675
Come on!

587
00:48:06,463 --> 00:48:09,727
From now on, come out
and eat with me at mealtimes.

588
00:48:09,727 --> 00:48:12,526
- People need to eat to live.
- I do eat.

589
00:48:12,526 --> 00:48:15,847
I mean real meals. Not random
snacks you use to get by.

590
00:48:15,847 --> 00:48:18,015
A warm meal!

591
00:48:18,015 --> 00:48:20,523
I eat proper meals sometimes.

592
00:48:20,523 --> 00:48:23,591
And after we eat,
take a walk in the park with me.

593
00:48:23,591 --> 00:48:25,024
- What?
- Don't just hole up

594
00:48:25,024 --> 00:48:26,639
in that smelly little room.

595
00:48:26,639 --> 00:48:29,559
Get some fresh air once in a while, okay?

596
00:48:30,403 --> 00:48:32,027
I do, sometimes.

597
00:48:32,027 --> 00:48:35,359
After our walk, let's go clothes shopping.

598
00:48:37,627 --> 00:48:41,092
You look like you've got a decent frame.

599
00:48:43,851 --> 00:48:46,863
Oh, I dress pretty well.

600
00:48:46,863 --> 00:48:49,031
This is all for my sake.

601
00:48:49,031 --> 00:48:52,495
Now that Director Yoo is gone,
who knows how often we'll go out together?

602
00:48:52,495 --> 00:48:54,692
So take good care of your condition.

603
00:48:59,855 --> 00:49:02,435
What are you doing? It'll get cold.

604
00:49:02,435 --> 00:49:04,135
Okay.

605
00:49:14,787 --> 00:49:17,171
Mommy.

606
00:49:17,171 --> 00:49:19,735
Mommy.

607
00:49:19,735 --> 00:49:21,927
Mommy.

608
00:49:21,927 --> 00:49:24,731
- Where are you, Mommy?
- Yul, what's wrong?

609
00:49:24,731 --> 00:49:27,826
When is Mommy coming?

610
00:49:30,175 --> 00:49:31,695
Yul,

611
00:49:31,695 --> 00:49:35,335
Mommy has so much work,
so she isn't finished yet.

612
00:49:35,335 --> 00:49:38,795
I miss Mommy,

613
00:49:38,795 --> 00:49:41,983
but I guess she doesn't miss me.

614
00:49:41,983 --> 00:49:44,251
Oh, no, that's not true.

615
00:49:44,251 --> 00:49:47,651
Mommy misses you so much,
so she cries every night.

616
00:49:47,651 --> 00:49:48,707
Really?

617
00:49:48,707 --> 00:49:51,307
Of course. It's true.

618
00:49:51,307 --> 00:49:52,892
Yul,

619
00:49:52,892 --> 00:49:58,023
Mommy also misses you,
but she's being strong and working hard.

620
00:49:58,023 --> 00:50:00,226
So what should Yul do?

621
00:50:01,815 --> 00:50:04,487
Yul should be brave and behave, right?

622
00:50:04,487 --> 00:50:06,892
That way, when Mommy comes home...

623
00:50:08,308 --> 00:50:12,535
When she comes home, wow,
she'll be so happy and say,

624
00:50:12,535 --> 00:50:15,759
"Wow, my Yul waited
so bravely for me," right?

625
00:50:16,783 --> 00:50:21,299
Until then, Yul will play,
eat, and sleep well.

626
00:50:21,299 --> 00:50:23,419
And Daddy will work hard.

627
00:50:23,419 --> 00:50:28,247
And we'll wait bravely for Mommy together.

628
00:50:28,247 --> 00:50:29,947
How's that?

629
00:50:34,863 --> 00:50:36,892
That's my good girl, Yul.

630
00:50:43,659 --> 00:50:45,226
[Siem Reap Mom-Daughter
Murder Case Relationship Chart]

631
00:50:45,226 --> 00:50:46,459
[July 24, 2025, Oh Seong Nam
and Han Deok Man entered Siem Reap]

632
00:50:46,459 --> 00:50:47,826
[Oh Seong Nam, Han Deok Man,
What is their connection? Tourism?]

633
00:50:47,826 --> 00:50:49,592
[Checklist, Inquire with local guides,
Find their connection]

634
00:50:52,326 --> 00:50:53,926
[Oh Seong Nam and Han Deok Man,
Need to verify the relationship]

635
00:50:53,926 --> 00:50:57,126
[Dark Web Bypass]

636
00:51:00,095 --> 00:51:01,095
[Oh Seong Nam Orthopedic Clinic]
Huh?

637
00:51:01,095 --> 00:51:02,451
[Onsang Middle School]
Huh?

638
00:51:02,451 --> 00:51:05,795
Mr. Kwon! Please take a look at this!

639
00:51:05,795 --> 00:51:08,623
You see Dr. Oh and Child Love here?

640
00:51:08,623 --> 00:51:11,107
It's an illegal site. Right here.

641
00:51:11,107 --> 00:51:12,459
This is evidence related to the case.

642
00:51:12,459 --> 00:51:16,143
It was faxed over to us
by the Cambodian police.

643
00:51:16,143 --> 00:51:18,915
Please check it just once.

644
00:51:18,915 --> 00:51:20,687
The chicken porridge is here.

645
00:51:20,687 --> 00:51:22,792
Wow, that looks good.

646
00:51:28,223 --> 00:51:31,350
- Mommy likes chicken porridge too.
- Right?

647
00:51:31,350 --> 00:51:32,879
- Mommy loves chicken porridge, right?
- Yeah.

648
00:51:32,879 --> 00:51:35,432
- Yeah.
- Is Daddy a good cook?

649
00:51:35,432 --> 00:51:36,455
You're pretty good.

650
00:51:36,455 --> 00:51:38,155
Thank you.

651
00:51:44,223 --> 00:51:46,355
Daddy, I'm all done cleaning up!

652
00:51:46,355 --> 00:51:47,575
Did you clean this all up yourself, Yul?

653
00:51:47,575 --> 00:51:49,692
- Yeah.
- Great job.

654
00:52:02,259 --> 00:52:03,903
[Exclusive: Kingfisher's Final Two Victims
Were Not Innocent Civilians]

655
00:52:03,903 --> 00:52:06,419
<i>Kingfisher's last two victims</i>

656
00:52:06,419 --> 00:52:08,592
<i>were not innocent civilians.</i>

657
00:52:09,435 --> 00:52:12,587
<i>The shocking truth about the two men</i>

658
00:52:12,587 --> 00:52:15,559
<i>believed to be Kingfisher's
final victims has finally come to light.</i>

659
00:52:15,559 --> 00:52:17,124
[Kingfisher's Final Two Victims]
<i>The two men, previously</i>

660
00:52:17,124 --> 00:52:18,911
[Exposed as Criminals]
<i>believed to have no connection,</i>

661
00:52:18,911 --> 00:52:20,643
<i>were confirmed to have stayed</i>

662
00:52:20,643 --> 00:52:24,163
<i>in the same Southeast Asian country
during the same period in the past.</i>

663
00:52:24,163 --> 00:52:28,314
<i>An investigation based on a tip
from a Korean media outlet</i>

664
00:52:28,314 --> 00:52:31,611
<i>and cooperation from local authorities
uncovered their plot</i>

665
00:52:31,611 --> 00:52:33,867
<i>and the murder of a mom and daughter.</i>

666
00:52:33,867 --> 00:52:37,055
<i>According to a joint investigation
by the media and police,</i>

667
00:52:37,055 --> 00:52:40,271
<i>the two men lured an eight-year-old girl</i>

668
00:52:40,271 --> 00:52:44,899
<i>selling food on the street
in a Southeast Asian country.</i>

669
00:52:44,899 --> 00:52:47,095
<i>When the girl's mom resisted
their attempt to sexually assault her,</i>

670
00:52:47,095 --> 00:52:49,439
<i>they brutally murdered both mom and daughter</i>

671
00:52:49,439 --> 00:52:52,043
<i>and disposed of their bodies.</i>

672
00:52:52,043 --> 00:52:55,535
<i>The two men, a practicing doctor
and a middle school teacher,</i>

673
00:52:55,535 --> 00:52:57,715
<i>were members of an illegal website</i>

674
00:52:57,715 --> 00:53:00,415
<i>sharing child sexual exploitation material.</i>

675
00:53:00,415 --> 00:53:02,955
<i>They met offline to plot the crime,</i>

676
00:53:02,955 --> 00:53:06,887
<i>and then pretended
to travel abroad separately</i>

677
00:53:06,887 --> 00:53:10,811
<i>before meeting there to carry it out.</i>

678
00:53:10,811 --> 00:53:12,665
Alright, everyone.

679
00:53:12,665 --> 00:53:13,767
Let's head out.

680
00:53:13,767 --> 00:53:15,535
Let's go!

681
00:53:15,535 --> 00:53:16,774
Let's go!

682
00:53:16,774 --> 00:53:18,474
Okay.

683
00:53:23,623 --> 00:53:24,887
What about Tae Min?

684
00:53:24,887 --> 00:53:25,891
Oh.

685
00:53:25,891 --> 00:53:27,759
Have a safe trip.

686
00:53:36,275 --> 00:53:41,107
<i>As the shocking crimes of the two men</i>

687
00:53:41,107 --> 00:53:43,326
<i>once believed to be innocent victims
of Kingfisher come to light,</i>

688
00:53:43,326 --> 00:53:46,559
<i>public opinion on Kingfisher
is changing again.</i>

689
00:53:46,559 --> 00:53:50,171
<i>"Kingfisher never hurt
innocent people after all."</i>

690
00:53:50,171 --> 00:53:52,426
<i>"I always believed in him..."</i>

691
00:53:54,903 --> 00:53:56,603
Look at him.

692
00:53:57,743 --> 00:54:01,226
He finally cleared Kingfisher's name.

693
00:54:31,075 --> 00:54:34,359
I need to clean up that place too.

694
00:54:43,287 --> 00:54:45,492
I wonder how Yoo Bo Na's story

695
00:54:46,795 --> 00:54:48,592
will end.

696
00:54:56,671 --> 00:54:59,243
Yul, Daddy is working late today,

697
00:54:59,243 --> 00:55:01,431
[6 Months Later]
so Auntie Se Ah will pick you up.

698
00:55:01,431 --> 00:55:02,494
Okay?

699
00:55:02,494 --> 00:55:05,019
Wash your hands as soon as you get home.

700
00:55:05,019 --> 00:55:09,711
Daddy made your favorite curry.
Eat up with Auntie Se Ah.

701
00:55:09,711 --> 00:55:12,003
My little precious,
you can do that for me, right?

702
00:55:12,003 --> 00:55:14,510
Yeah, I can.

703
00:55:14,510 --> 00:55:15,547
That's my Yul. You're the best.

704
00:55:15,547 --> 00:55:17,287
The best! The best!

705
00:55:17,287 --> 00:55:19,555
Mommy used to do it like this.

706
00:55:19,555 --> 00:55:21,469
The best! The best!

707
00:55:21,469 --> 00:55:23,392
Mommy did that?

708
00:55:24,995 --> 00:55:28,459
Huh? It's snowing. Daddy, look, it's snowing!

709
00:55:28,459 --> 00:55:30,592
Wow, snow!

710
00:55:38,903 --> 00:55:40,892
Want to go outside and see?

711
00:55:44,587 --> 00:55:48,667
Wow, there's so much white snow.

712
00:55:48,667 --> 00:55:51,864
It sure is. The first snow
came early this year.

713
00:55:51,864 --> 00:55:53,959
Wow, it's beautiful.

714
00:56:00,219 --> 00:56:03,215
My name is Yoo Bo Na. It's my real name.

715
00:56:03,215 --> 00:56:06,592
Please take good care of me.
It's my first time with love.

716
00:56:12,591 --> 00:56:14,291
It's beautiful.

717
00:57:03,887 --> 00:57:06,547
Any idea where she might have gone?

718
00:57:06,547 --> 00:57:08,639
I'm not sure.

719
00:57:08,639 --> 00:57:11,059
She's always been good at hiding.

720
00:57:11,859 --> 00:57:13,892
She's probably somewhere

721
00:57:14,592 --> 00:57:17,063
finding a view of her own.

722
00:57:17,063 --> 00:57:19,132
But three or four months later,

723
00:57:19,132 --> 00:57:20,747
she came back and asked us
to tear up her resignation.

724
00:57:20,747 --> 00:57:23,127
I asked her why.

725
00:57:23,127 --> 00:57:25,656
And she only said one thing.

726
00:57:25,656 --> 00:57:28,763
"I've seen a beautiful view."

727
00:57:28,763 --> 00:57:33,126
I wondered what beautiful view
she'd seen, and where,

728
00:57:33,126 --> 00:57:37,592
that brought someone who was
practically dead back to life like that.

729
00:57:39,715 --> 00:57:42,226
Seeing you, Mr. Kwon Tae Seong,
made me realize it.

730
00:57:42,226 --> 00:57:44,051
It was you.

731
00:57:44,051 --> 00:57:46,892
<i>You are the one who saved Director Yoo.</i>

732
00:58:36,991 --> 00:58:39,127
She never used to step outside.

733
00:58:39,127 --> 00:58:41,691
So I don't know what got into her
to go to the mountains.

734
00:58:41,691 --> 00:58:43,907
On a day like this too.

735
00:58:43,907 --> 00:58:46,026
The trail must be rough.

736
00:59:08,411 --> 00:59:10,751
<i>Merry Christmas!</i>

737
00:59:10,751 --> 00:59:15,092
This is a Christmas present for you, Bo Na!

738
00:59:16,145 --> 00:59:18,759
Aren't they beautiful and crystal clear?

739
00:59:19,739 --> 00:59:22,516
When I was little, I used to suck on them.

740
00:59:22,516 --> 00:59:25,159
We could make shaved ice with them, right?

741
00:59:30,851 --> 00:59:33,083
I was so scared.

742
00:59:33,083 --> 00:59:35,865
I was afraid you might disappear.

743
00:59:35,865 --> 00:59:38,348
Perhaps love begins

744
00:59:38,348 --> 00:59:40,111
when you find yourself drawn to

745
00:59:40,111 --> 00:59:43,355
just one side of a person
among all the many sides they have.

746
00:59:43,355 --> 00:59:45,592
<i>I've already fallen in love.</i>

747
01:00:14,839 --> 01:00:16,539
It's beautiful.

748
01:00:18,883 --> 01:00:21,939
This place is really
more beautiful in winter.

749
01:00:21,939 --> 01:00:23,639
Don't you think?

750
01:00:28,026 --> 01:00:30,539
This wildflower field
used to be the view of my life.

751
01:00:30,539 --> 01:00:33,671
But since then,
it has changed into a snowfield.

752
01:00:33,671 --> 01:00:38,343
I guess even your taste in scenery changes
depending on who you're with.

753
01:00:38,343 --> 01:00:40,892
If the flowers heard that,
would they feel a little hurt?

754
01:00:46,711 --> 01:00:50,041
The trail was rough,
so it took me forever to get up here.

755
01:00:50,041 --> 01:00:55,379
I was worried they'd close
the road because of the snow.

756
01:00:55,379 --> 01:00:57,926
But luckily, the mountain let me through.

757
01:00:58,575 --> 01:01:00,492
I slipped twice, though.

758
01:01:00,492 --> 01:01:04,559
I was in such a rush,
so I didn't bring the right shoes.

759
01:01:09,519 --> 01:01:11,219
I thought...

760
01:01:14,275 --> 01:01:17,025
I didn't need to know.

761
01:01:17,025 --> 01:01:19,492
Where you were born, how you grew up,

762
01:01:19,492 --> 01:01:22,651
what you do, how you live...

763
01:01:22,651 --> 01:01:24,691
I thought it was okay
not knowing any of that.

764
01:01:24,691 --> 01:01:27,426
Because the Yoo Bo Na I know
was enough for me.

765
01:01:28,167 --> 01:01:30,959
You eat chicken
and chicken porridge well now.

766
01:01:31,626 --> 01:01:35,807
And you tell Yul every day
to get along with her friends.

767
01:01:35,807 --> 01:01:37,507
You've got a mom

768
01:01:38,395 --> 01:01:41,971
and three sisters-in-law.

769
01:01:41,971 --> 01:01:44,059
You're not alone anymore.

770
01:01:45,812 --> 01:01:47,959
I know you so well now.

771
01:01:49,227 --> 01:01:53,126
And I love you more than
anyone in this world.

772
01:01:56,471 --> 01:01:58,526
But now I want to know.

773
01:02:01,292 --> 01:02:04,959
What was in your heart
as you walked that long road.

774
01:02:04,959 --> 01:02:07,551
How difficult it was.

775
01:02:07,551 --> 01:02:10,624
Whether you were lonely or scared. All of it.

776
01:02:10,624 --> 01:02:13,526
Every side of you that I don't know.

777
01:02:21,326 --> 01:02:24,026
I know we can't go back to how things were.

778
01:02:25,151 --> 01:02:26,775
But let's do this instead.

779
01:02:26,775 --> 01:02:28,859
Let's take our time
getting to know each other.

780
01:02:29,481 --> 01:02:31,181
Okay?

781
01:02:36,975 --> 01:02:39,959
So I can learn to love every side of you.

782
01:02:59,692 --> 01:03:02,383
Come home with me.

783
01:03:02,383 --> 01:03:04,459
It's freezing here.

784
01:03:09,187 --> 01:03:11,192
Yul's waiting for you too.

785
01:03:16,792 --> 01:03:20,559
I told her a wish
on the first snowfall comes true,

786
01:03:21,891 --> 01:03:24,726
and she wished to see her mommy.

787
01:03:25,647 --> 01:03:27,492
Just like me.

788
01:04:11,987 --> 01:04:14,192
There's something I've always wondered.

789
01:04:15,633 --> 01:04:17,333
What is it?

790
01:04:22,199 --> 01:04:23,771
Back during the World Cup...

791
01:04:23,771 --> 01:04:24,771
Yeah.

792
01:04:24,771 --> 01:04:27,035
Why did you report it for me?

793
01:04:27,035 --> 01:04:28,826
Because you were handsome

794
01:04:31,844 --> 01:04:33,859
and seemed like a good person.

795
01:04:37,926 --> 01:04:42,026
[Tae Seong Chicken]

796
01:04:45,026 --> 01:04:48,092
[Tae Seong Chicken]

797
01:05:03,007 --> 01:05:05,275
Good grief.

798
01:05:05,275 --> 01:05:08,507
Why are you always cleaning
whenever you get a chance?

799
01:05:08,507 --> 01:05:10,047
Are you still that thrilled?

800
01:05:10,047 --> 01:05:11,791
Of course, I am.

801
01:05:11,791 --> 01:05:14,324
It feels like I have everything in the world.

802
01:05:14,324 --> 01:05:17,479
Honestly, the more I think about it,
he's the landlord type.

803
01:05:17,479 --> 01:05:21,035
I mean, how could he sell
this place at that price?

804
01:05:21,035 --> 01:05:22,419
Exactly.

805
01:05:22,419 --> 01:05:25,763
We should be grateful he never
raised the rent all those years.

806
01:05:25,763 --> 01:05:28,155
Such a wonderful person.

807
01:05:28,155 --> 01:05:32,387
I thought we'd finally meet at the signing,
but he never showed up.

808
01:05:32,387 --> 01:05:34,087
I know.

809
01:05:34,847 --> 01:05:36,547
Oh, my.

810
01:05:37,163 --> 01:05:39,871
You used to say your whole life
was in this shop.

811
01:05:39,871 --> 01:05:42,555
And now your life is truly
in full bloom in your golden years, right?

812
01:05:42,555 --> 01:05:46,342
Absolutely. It's really my shop now.

813
01:05:46,342 --> 01:05:49,039
I'm putting my whole life into this!

814
01:05:49,039 --> 01:05:50,175
All in!

815
01:05:50,175 --> 01:05:52,459
Oh, is that so?

816
01:05:54,643 --> 01:05:56,642
Mom! We're going to be late.

817
01:05:56,642 --> 01:05:58,531
Oh, goodness, I almost forgot...

818
01:05:58,531 --> 01:06:00,820
Hold on, we should get going.

819
01:06:00,820 --> 01:06:03,843
You packed plenty of
snacks and drinks, right?

820
01:06:03,843 --> 01:06:05,375
- Tons of them.
- Okay.

821
01:06:05,375 --> 01:06:07,075
Let's hurry.

822
01:06:08,959 --> 01:06:11,159
Let's go!

823
01:06:13,559 --> 01:06:15,159
[Closed This Morning Due to a Family Event]

824
01:06:15,159 --> 01:06:17,459
[Exciting Sports Day]

825
01:06:21,533 --> 01:06:23,532
[Kwon Yul]
Yul!

826
01:06:23,532 --> 01:06:27,019
- Oh, there's Yul!
- Go, Kwon Yul! Fighting!

827
01:06:27,019 --> 01:06:29,199
Wow!

828
01:06:29,199 --> 01:06:31,319
Go, Blue Team!

829
01:06:31,319 --> 01:06:33,019
[We Love You, Ji An]
Hye Ri!

830
01:06:33,992 --> 01:06:35,026
Faster, faster!

831
01:06:35,026 --> 01:06:36,059
That's it!

832
01:06:36,059 --> 01:06:38,199
Come on, come on!

833
01:06:38,199 --> 01:06:40,392
Wow!

834
01:06:40,392 --> 01:06:42,226
[My Family's Little Precious]

835
01:06:42,859 --> 01:06:44,426
First place!

836
01:06:44,426 --> 01:06:45,926
Mommy, I got first place!

837
01:06:45,926 --> 01:06:47,992
- That's my girl! You're the best!
- First place!

838
01:06:47,992 --> 01:06:49,119
My little precious is the best!

839
01:06:49,119 --> 01:06:51,990
See? My national athlete blood runs deep.

840
01:06:51,990 --> 01:06:53,895
Why would your blood go to her?

841
01:06:53,895 --> 01:06:56,751
Oh, my. I guess she's so happy
with Mommy and Daddy here.

842
01:06:56,751 --> 01:06:58,992
My Yul is flying around all giddy today too!

843
01:06:58,992 --> 01:07:00,930
Kwon Yul is the best!

844
01:07:00,930 --> 01:07:04,926
Next up is the parents' relay race.

845
01:07:07,714 --> 01:07:10,611
See the calf muscles on number one
from the other team?

846
01:07:10,611 --> 01:07:12,523
- Yeah.
- She does

847
01:07:12,523 --> 01:07:13,792
PT at least three times a week.

848
01:07:13,792 --> 01:07:14,855
- Three times...
- Three...

849
01:07:14,855 --> 01:07:16,599
She's got a fast start.

850
01:07:16,599 --> 01:07:17,835
And runner number two.

851
01:07:17,835 --> 01:07:19,599
She keeps taking the weight onto
her left leg, right?

852
01:07:19,599 --> 01:07:21,807
- Her knee's bothering her.
- Okay.

853
01:07:21,807 --> 01:07:23,003
Oh!

854
01:07:23,003 --> 01:07:25,423
She'll lose speed on the turns.

855
01:07:25,423 --> 01:07:28,235
Runner number three is especially dangerous.

856
01:07:28,235 --> 01:07:30,848
- Why?
- Why?

857
01:07:30,848 --> 01:07:32,852
[Sol's Mom! Fighting!]
Sol's mom! Fighting!

858
01:07:32,852 --> 01:07:34,463
- Mommy!
- Good job!

859
01:07:34,463 --> 01:07:37,051
People like that are insanely competitive.

860
01:07:37,051 --> 01:07:39,795
Her eyes will go wild
the second she gets the baton.

861
01:07:39,795 --> 01:07:42,399
And runner number five over there.

862
01:07:42,399 --> 01:07:45,026
She arrived in heels
and just changed into sneakers.

863
01:07:45,026 --> 01:07:46,847
Oh, no.

864
01:07:46,847 --> 01:07:50,775
That literally screams,

865
01:07:50,775 --> 01:07:52,835
"You're all dead meat today."

866
01:07:52,835 --> 01:07:55,447
Okay, then I'll take the last leg.

867
01:07:55,447 --> 01:07:57,343
I'm an expert at killing it.

868
01:07:57,343 --> 01:07:59,047
Okay!

869
01:07:59,047 --> 01:08:00,123
Alright, okay!

870
01:08:00,123 --> 01:08:01,159
Shall we do this?

871
01:08:01,159 --> 01:08:02,515
- Let's crush them!
- Let's crush them!

872
01:08:02,515 --> 01:08:04,215
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

873
01:08:05,959 --> 01:08:08,792
- Let's go!
- It's okay even if you lose.

874
01:08:14,026 --> 01:08:17,192
[Red Team, Blue Team]

875
01:08:19,643 --> 01:08:21,343
Ready...

876
01:08:27,159 --> 01:08:28,959
[Run, You Got This!]

877
01:08:31,515 --> 01:08:33,215
Take it!

878
01:08:36,323 --> 01:08:38,992
- Hye Ri's mom!
- Hye Ri's mom, please!

879
01:08:43,226 --> 01:08:44,926
[Sol's Mom! Fighting!]

880
01:08:47,035 --> 01:08:49,492
- Go, Seo Jun's mom!
- Go, Seo Jun's mom!

881
01:08:51,831 --> 01:08:53,626
Isn't she a little slow?

882
01:08:53,626 --> 01:08:54,626
What's she doing?

883
01:08:54,626 --> 01:08:56,323
- Wait...
- Gosh.

884
01:08:56,323 --> 01:08:57,892
She was just all talk.

885
01:08:57,892 --> 01:08:59,647
- Alright, good!
- Let's go!

886
01:08:59,647 --> 01:09:00,659
That's it.

887
01:09:00,659 --> 01:09:01,959
Good, let's go!

888
01:09:01,959 --> 01:09:03,691
- Let's go! Run!
- You got this!

889
01:09:03,691 --> 01:09:05,391
Let's go!

890
01:09:18,459 --> 01:09:20,326
[Exciting Sports Day]

891
01:09:20,326 --> 01:09:22,026
[A Celebration of Young Dreams]

892
01:09:24,192 --> 01:09:25,926
[Rooting for You]

893
01:09:40,207 --> 01:09:41,551
Wow! At an incredible speed...

894
01:09:41,551 --> 01:09:43,403
- What happened to her?
- The final runner is charging ahead.

895
01:09:43,403 --> 01:09:45,391
She's closing the gap.

896
01:09:45,391 --> 01:09:47,483
- Go, Yoo Bo Na!
- And now, the final runner...

897
01:09:47,483 --> 01:09:50,326
- One more lap!
- Go, Mommy!

898
01:10:07,626 --> 01:10:09,226
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

899
01:10:09,226 --> 01:10:11,026
Wow!

900
01:10:22,203 --> 01:10:23,926
What did I just see?

901
01:10:23,926 --> 01:10:26,026
Yul got it from her mommy.

902
01:10:26,026 --> 01:10:28,859
What did she do back in the day?

903
01:10:28,859 --> 01:10:31,126
That's some serious
wasted talent in every way.

904
01:10:31,126 --> 01:10:35,526
I'm so proud of my daughter-in-law!

905
01:10:48,451 --> 01:10:50,151
Good grief.

906
01:10:53,371 --> 01:10:55,626
- Jeez.
- Wow!

907
01:10:56,491 --> 01:10:57,615
Gosh, you scared me!

908
01:10:57,615 --> 01:11:00,467
Slacking off instead of working, huh?

909
01:11:00,467 --> 01:11:02,792
Oh, come on.

910
01:11:04,383 --> 01:11:06,592
I'm not slacking.

911
01:11:07,526 --> 01:11:09,947
I'm just taking a break from the sun.

912
01:11:09,947 --> 01:11:11,319
I thought I'd get roasted alive.

913
01:11:11,319 --> 01:11:13,763
So why do you keep making
life hard for yourself?

914
01:11:13,763 --> 01:11:16,626
Out of everyone on earth, you'd be
the first cop to turn down a promotion,

915
01:11:16,626 --> 01:11:19,707
a reward, and then volunteer to be demoted.

916
01:11:19,707 --> 01:11:21,015
Look who's talking!

917
01:11:21,015 --> 01:11:22,418
Then is it common for a reporter to refuse

918
01:11:22,418 --> 01:11:24,659
the "Journalist of the Year Award," huh?

919
01:11:27,031 --> 01:11:28,731
Jeez.

920
01:11:30,419 --> 01:11:32,787
There are still plenty of bad guys out there.

921
01:11:32,787 --> 01:11:35,963
That's why I'm taking all the heat.

922
01:11:35,963 --> 01:11:38,091
People are demanding Kingfisher back.

923
01:11:38,091 --> 01:11:42,339
People always miss things that don't exist.

924
01:11:42,339 --> 01:11:45,483
Jeez, they should look for that
in fantasy stories.

925
01:11:45,483 --> 01:11:48,659
So go back to your place
and do your job, okay?

926
01:11:48,659 --> 01:11:52,183
Make sure another one doesn't pop up!

927
01:11:52,183 --> 01:11:53,827
Of course, I will.

928
01:11:53,827 --> 01:11:55,527
Jeez.

929
01:11:58,351 --> 01:12:01,243
You do your job properly too, Kwon Tae Seong!

930
01:12:01,243 --> 01:12:02,659
I always do.

931
01:12:02,659 --> 01:12:04,943
Unbelievable...

932
01:12:04,943 --> 01:12:06,692
Jeez.

933
01:12:36,026 --> 01:12:38,126
[Three Bears]

934
01:13:06,663 --> 01:13:08,391
<i>A woman in her 30s was found</i>

935
01:13:08,391 --> 01:13:12,067
<i>stabbed to death in a residential
neighborhood in Seoul this morning.</i>

936
01:13:12,067 --> 01:13:13,974
<i>Police say the man, in his 40s,</i>

937
01:13:13,974 --> 01:13:16,583
<i>had served time
for stalking the woman for years.</i>

938
01:13:16,583 --> 01:13:18,793
<i>They believe he killed her in retaliation</i>

939
01:13:18,793 --> 01:13:21,243
<i>after she reported him,
following his release,</i>

940
01:13:21,243 --> 01:13:24,467
<i>and are currently searching
for the suspect, who fled the scene.</i>

941
01:13:24,467 --> 01:13:26,451
<i>The victim reportedly
told people close to her</i>

942
01:13:26,451 --> 01:13:28,887
<i>that she feared he would come
after her once he was released.</i>

943
01:13:28,887 --> 01:13:30,789
[Victim Reportedly Feared Retaliation]
<i>She was said to have been</i>

944
01:13:30,789 --> 01:13:32,699
[After His Release]
<i>extremely distressed.</i>

945
01:13:32,699 --> 01:13:35,747
<i>As public concern grows over
recurring retaliatory crimes,</i>

946
01:13:35,747 --> 01:13:39,792
<i>police are focusing their efforts
on apprehending the suspect.</i>

947
01:13:40,647 --> 01:13:42,347
Yeah.

948
01:13:45,147 --> 01:13:47,892
Okay. Shall we go?

949
01:15:44,426 --> 01:15:46,176
[Thank you to all our viewers!]

950
01:15:46,176 --> 01:15:48,526
[May you all find your own beautiful view!]

